       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose there's a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and QT prolongation. Normal kidney and liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **100 mg** by mouth once daily. This is a common maintenance dose.\n- **50 mg** by mouth once daily. This is the usual starting dose for depression and anxiety.\n- **200 mg** by mouth once daily. This is the maximum dose.\n\nTell me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away. If 1000 mg really is intended, for example as a deliberate exception, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
